    {
      "id": "claim_d3c0b63bcdd446b9b1fe8e28af20eec7",
      "statement": "The deepagents.middleware package re-exports its public middleware classes and supporting types for filesystem, summarization, skills (including SkillToolResolver), subagents, async subagents, memory, rubric, and unsupported content from its __init__.py, defining the surface consumers import from deepagents.middleware.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/deepagents/deepagents/middleware/__init__.py",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:b93b885b634bcbfe92fca651305a7e6aecb4f4c1e5da9c632292422a606ce05f"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_408faefac079476e9300895e10e35bbe",
      "statement": "Middleware subclasses AgentMiddleware and overrides hooks such as wrap_model_call() that intercept every LLM request before it is sent, letting it filter tools, inject system-prompt context, transform messages, and maintain cross-turn state — capabilities a plain tools= callable (invoked only after the model calls it) cannot provide.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/deepagents/deepagents/middleware/__init__.py",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:b93b885b634bcbfe92fca651305a7e6aecb4f4c1e5da9c632292422a606ce05f"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3748cc5f2e584ab3ac271a270b94ece8",
      "statement": "SkillsMiddleware implements Anthropic's agent skills pattern with progressive disclosure, loading skills from one or more backend sources (later sources overriding earlier by name) and injecting instructions into the system prompt using backend APIs only.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/deepagents/deepagents/middleware/skills.py",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:f3cc2139f2b77bd599bf99df032efe27774462b2ecc80f6e58b7ea7edd2d7895"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_396d990889144e2cbefe1c93b616197b",
      "statement": "Graph construction builds a core stack of filesystem, optional synchronous subagents, summarization, tool-call repair, and optional asynchronous subagents; profile middleware, optional skills, provider caching, optional memory, HITL, and unsupported-content filtering form the tail. Caller middleware replaces a same-named entry in place or otherwise lands after the core, and profile-controlled tool exclusion is appended last.",
